<BaseLayout title='About | Trouvus' description='Trouvus closes the gap between AI possibility and organizational reality through research-grounded transformation.'>
<Hero eyebrow="About Trouvus" title="Closing the gap between AI possibility and organizational reality." lead="Trouvus integrates research, strategy, organizational design and implementation discipline to help leaders make consequential technology decisions." variant="network" /><section><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Where research meets implementation.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Trouvus was founded by Dr. Mitt Nowshade Kabir to translate advances in AI, digital transformation and technology management into practical business-model, operating-model and workforce decisions.</p><p>The firm’s perspective draws on management scholarship, entrepreneurship, executive education and investment-side analysis. This multidisciplinary foundation enables Trouvus to examine not only whether a technology works, but where it creates value, how it changes work and what organizational capabilities are required to sustain it.</p><p>Recent teaching and investment work—including analysis through MIOS—adds an explicit capital-allocation lens: attractive technology is not automatically an attractive transformation investment.</p></div></div></section><section class="rule"><div class="wrap split"><div><div class="eyebrow">Founder</div><h2>Dr. Mitt Nowshade Kabir</h2></div><div><p class="lead">An AI and digital-transformation strategist, serial entrepreneur and academic with more than three decades of experience at the intersection of emerging technology, innovation and business strategy.</p><p>Dr. Kabir holds a Ph.D. in Information Technology, a Doctorate in Business Administration, an M.Sc. in Computer Science and an MBA. He is the author of <a class="source-link" href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1057/978-1-137-34809-8" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Knowledge-Based Social Entrepreneurship</em></a> (Palgrave Macmillan) and has published more than thirty peer-reviewed research papers spanning AI strategy, generative-AI governance, human-AI co-creation, knowledge management and digital transformation.</p><p>He has served as an Adjunct Professor of Digital Transformation, chaired the European Conference on the Impact of Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (ECIAIR), and advised governments, boards and businesses on advanced technologies, business development and innovation strategy. As an entrepreneur he has founded and built technology ventures in e-commerce and enterprise software across international markets.</p><div class="grid-2"><Card title="Research" text="30+ peer-reviewed papers; author, <em>Knowledge-Based Social Entrepreneurship</em> (Palgrave Macmillan)." /><Card title="Teaching" text="Adjunct Professor of Digital Transformation; executive education for leadership teams." /><Card title="Academic leadership" text="Programme Chair, European Conference on the Impact of AI and Robotics (ECIAIR)." /><Card title="Investment perspective" text="Technology and transformation choices examined through enterprise value, risk and capital discipline." /></div></div></div></section><section class="rule"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Operating principles</div><div class="grid-3"><Card icon="icon-evidence" title="Evidence before enthusiasm" text="We distinguish demonstrated capability, informed inference and unproven promise." /><Card icon="icon-strategy" title="Strategy before technology" text="We start with the decision, value logic and operating context." /><Card icon="icon-workforce" title="Capability before scale" text="Transformation becomes durable when ownership and competence exist inside the organization." /><Card icon="icon-bizmodel" title="Human agency alongside automation" text="Critical judgment and adaptive capacity must remain load-bearing organizational assets." /><Card icon="icon-implementation" title="Measurable outcomes over activity" text="Workshops, pilots and systems are means; business and organizational outcomes are the test." /><Card icon="icon-diagnose" title="Responsible transformation by design" text="Governance, risk and accountability should be built into the operating model." /></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="quote">“AI transformation succeeds when strategy, operating processes, technology, governance and human capability are redesigned together.”</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
